  "observations": [
    "The pilot media frame and the non-pilot consumer share identical chip primitives (.case-media__label, .case-media__kind, .case-media__kind-dot: rgb(21,21,19) on rgb(255,255,255), 8.32px mono, 999px radius) while their frame chrome differs per project (Keshi rgb(9,9,9) / rgba(255,248,236,0.16) / 12.48px radius vs Zucchini rgb(5,5,5) / rgba(255,255,255,0.44) / 15.2px radius). That split is exactly what a semantic-token migration must preserve.",
    ".case-keshi-state__caption renders with padding 0, transparent background and no backdrop-filter: KeshiLiquidGlass.css neutralises it into a layout-only slot. Its declared padding/border/background/backdrop-filter rules in ProjectDetailsStories.css are dead for this route.",
    "At 390x844 the fixed MENU control overlaps the section heading text. Pre-existing, outside the pilot scope, recorded so it is not later mistaken for a harness regression."
  ],
